":"video/mp4","url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2083744791876292608/vid/avc1/1920x1080/9NW2QWX_Ejzzlpj5.mp4?tag=29"}]}}]}},"note_tweet":{"is_expandable":true,"note_tweet_results":{"result":{"entity_set":{"hashtags":[],"symbols":[],"urls":[],"user_mentions":[]},"text":"We're starting to leave the territory where you'd test an LLM by e.g. \"create an svg of pelican on a bicycle\". As one idea to generalize it, I was interested what Opus 5 would do if I gave it the first paragraph of the Lord of the Rings, a 1M token budget (~$10) and asked for three js render of it. Opus went off for ~2 hours and wrote 5500 lines of code that (procedurally) rendered the story. It's kind of janky but fun.\n\nLast thought is that the domain of worlds/games exposes a weakness in LLMs."}}},"views":{"count":"6056007"}}]
